Accessing Properties of Graphic Shapes
12-1010 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BoardMaterialActive [SimTalk]
Activates (true) or deactivates (false) the material of the boards of the rack designated by <Path>.
Remarks
You cannot assign BoardMaterialActive when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or
when the graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.BoardMaterialActive:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
.Models.MyModel._3D.getGraphic("deco", [4]).BoardMaterialActive := true
See also
Rack > Rack Settings BoardMaterialEmissiveColor [SimTalk]
createRack [SimTalk] BoardMaterialShininess [SimTalk]
_Rack Attributes BoardMaterialSpecularColor [SimTalk]
BoardMaterialAmbientColor [SimTalk] BoardMaterialTransparency [SimTalk]
BoardMaterialDiffuseColor [SimTalk] _3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
BoardMaterialActive [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1011
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BoardMaterialAmbientColor [SimTalk]
Sets the ambient color of the board material of the rack designated by <Path>.
Remarks
When assigning a value to the attribute, we automatically set the material to active
(MaterialActive := true).
You cannot assign the attribute when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or when the
graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
You can only access the attribute if the material is active.
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.BoardMaterialAmbientColor:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
You will usually set the color with the method makeRGBValue [SimTalk].
Example
.Models.MyModel._3D.getGraphic("deco", [5]).BoardMaterialAmbientColor := 
makeRGBValue(255,0,0)
See also
Rack > Rack Settings BoardMaterialEmissiveColor [SimTalk]
createRack [SimTalk] BoardMaterialShininess [SimTalk]
_Rack Attributes BoardMaterialSpecularColor [SimTalk]
BoardMaterialAmbientColor [SimTalk] BoardMaterialTransparency [SimTalk]
BoardMaterialDiffuseColor [SimTalk] _3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
BoardMaterialAmbientColor [SimTalk]
