Dimensioning
Dimensioning Attributes
12-1032 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

DimensioningSpace [SimTalk]
Sets the dimensioning space of the graphic designated by <Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.DimensioningSpace:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify "X Axis", "Y Axis", "Z Axis", or "XY plane".
Example
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).DimensioningSpace := "XY plane"
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).MeasuringPoint1 := [2,2,2]
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).MeasuringPoint2 := [3,4,5]
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).TextPosition := [6,6,6]
print .Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).MeasuredLength 
// returns 2.23606797749979m
See also
Insert Shape > Dimensioning MeasuringPoint2 [SimTalk]
createDimensioning [SimTalk] TextPosition [SimTalk]
MeasuredLength [SimTalk] getGraphic
MeasuringPoint1 [SimTalk]
DimensioningSpace [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1033
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

MeasuredLength [SimTalk]
Returns the length of the graphic designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The measuring text shows this length.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.MeasuredLength -> length
Return Value
The return value has the data type length.
Example
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).DimensioningSpace := "XY plane"
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).MeasuringPoint1 := [2,2,2]
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).MeasuringPoint2 := [3,4,5]
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).TextPosition := [6,6,6]
print .Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).MeasuredLength 
// returns 2.23606797749979m
See also
Insert Shape > Dimensioning MeasuringPoint2 [SimTalk]
createDimensioning [SimTalk] TextPosition [SimTalk]
DimensioningSpace [SimTalk] _3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
MeasuringPoint1 [SimTalk]
MeasuredLength [SimTalk]
12-1034 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

MeasuringPoint1 [SimTalk]
Sets the first measuring point of the graphic designated by <Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.MeasuringPoint1:length[3]
Assignment Value
You can assign an array of data type length with three values.
The values designate the X-Position, the Y-Position, and the Z-Position of the measuring point.
Example
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).DimensioningSpace := "XY plane"
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).MeasuringPoint1 := [2,2,2]
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).MeasuringPoint2 := [3,4,5]
.Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).TextPosition := [6,6,6]
print .Models.Model2._3D.getGraphic("deco", [2]).MeasuredLength 
// returns 2.23606797749979m
See also
Insert Shape > Dimensioning MeasuringPoint2 [SimTalk]
createDimensioning [SimTalk] TextPosition [SimTalk]
DimensioningSpace [SimTalk] _3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
MeasuredLength [SimTalk]
MeasuringPoint1 [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1035
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

