BayDepth [SimTalk]
Sets the depth of a single storage bay of the rack designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the attribute when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or when the
graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Note
The attribute BayDepth indirectly also sets the depth of the entire rack.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.BayDepth:length
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type length.
Example
MyFrame._3D.getGraphic("deco", [8]).BayDepth := 1.5
See also
Rack > Rack Settings
createRack [SimTalk]
_Rack Attributes
_3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
BayDepth [SimTalk]
12-1130 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

BaySize [SimTalk]
Sets the size of a single storage bay of the rack designated by <Path> in the XZ-dimension.
Remarks
The value for X or [0] returns the first value and the value for Y or [1] returns the second value although
the orientation in the X/Z-direction is defined from the point of view of the rack.
When you assign values to the attribute, the existing capacity does not change and the overall dimensions
of the storage bay, i.e., the values of the attribute Dimensions are changed as well.
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the attribute when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or when the
graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.BaySize:length[2]
Assignment Value
You can assign an array of data type length with two values.
Example
MyFrame._3D.getGraphic("deco", [8]).BaySize := [2, 2.5]
See also
Dimensions [SimTalk] - graphic
Rack > Rack Settings
createRack [SimTalk]
_Rack Attributes
_3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
BaySize [SimTalk]
