Capacity [SimTalk] - rack
Sets the number of storage bays per board and the number of boards of the rack designated by <Path> in
the XZ-Dimension.
Remarks
You can specify the storage bays per board in the X-direction (.X/[0]) and the number of boards in the
Y-direction (.Y/[1]).
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the attribute when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or when the
graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Capacity:integer[2]
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Assignment Value
You can assign an array of data type integer with two values.
Example
.Models.MyModel._3D.getGraphic("deco", [8]).Capacity := [4, 4]
See also
Rack > Rack Settings
createRack [SimTalk]
_Rack Attributes
_3D.getGraphic [SimTalk]
Capacity [SimTalk] - rack
12-1134 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

GroundClearance [SimTalk]
Sets the Ground Clearance of the rack designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The Ground Clearance is the distance between the lower edge of the lowest shelf and the floor on which
the rack stands.
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the attribute when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or when the
graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Note
This setting only applies for the Store Types > Rack with round/square posts (dynamic).
GroundClearance [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-1135
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.GroundClearance:length
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type length which sets the ground clearance.
Specify void to use the default ground clearance.
Specify 0 so that the lowest shelf rests flat on the floor.
Example
Store3._3D.StoreType := "Rack with round posts (dynamic)"
Store3._3D.Gap := 0.1
Store3._3D.FloorThickness := 0.15
Store3._3D.GroundClearance := 0.3
See also
Appearance of the Store > Ground Clearance
GroundClearance [SimTalk]
12-1136 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

