StringerMaterialEmissiveColor [SimTalk]
Sets the emissive color of the material of the stringers of the staircase designated by <Path>.
Remarks
When assigning a value to the attribute, we automatically set the material to active
(MaterialActive := true).
You can only access the attribute if the material is active.
Assigning the attribute deactivates graphic inheritance.
You cannot assign the attribute when the graphic is an automatically generated graphic group or when the
graphic is located in an automatically generated graphic group.
Note
The stringer material does not affect the handrails of the staircase.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.StringerMaterialEmissiveColor:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
You will usually set the color with the method makeRGBValue.
Example
.Models.MyModel._3D.getGraphic("deco", 
[5]).StringerMaterialEmissiveColor := makeRGBValue(255,0,0)
See also
Stairs > Stairs Settings StringerMaterialDiffuseColor
createRack [SimTalk] StringerMaterialShininess [SimTalk]
StringerMaterialEmissiveColor [SimTalk]
12-1164 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

